// ori_zeroext.hex
//
// BUG UNDER TEST
//   ori must zero-extend its immediate. MIPS splits the two cases by opcode
//   class: the logical immediates (ori, andi, xori) zero-extend, while the
//   arithmetic and memory immediates (addi, lw, sw) sign-extend. This core
//   routes every immediate through sign_extend, so
//
//       ori r7, r0, 0x8000
//
//   produces 0xFFFF8000 instead of 0x00008000. That is a wrong architectural
//   result for a legal instruction -- not a stall, not a timing cost, a wrong
//   number in a register.
//
// WHY BIT 15 MUST BE SET -- THE WHOLE TEST DEPENDS ON IT
//   Sign-extension and zero-extension differ ONLY in what fills bits [31:16],
//   and that filler is a copy of bit 15. For any immediate with bit 15 clear
//   the two are bit-for-bit identical, so a test using, say, 0x0044 passes
//   just as happily on the broken core as the fixed one and proves nothing
//   whatsoever.
//
//   The immediate here is 0x8000: bit 15 set, every other bit clear. That is
//   the minimal value that distinguishes the two extensions, and it makes the
//   failure maximally legible -- 0x00008000 against 0xFFFF8000, differing in
//   exactly the sixteen bits under test.
//
//   Any future edit to this program must keep bit 15 of the evidence immediate
//   set. Clearing it does not weaken the test, it silently disables it.
//
// EVIDENCE
//   r7 = 0x00008000. Nothing after index 0 writes it.
//
// POSITIVE CONTROL
//   r8 = 0x00000044, an ori with bit 15 CLEAR, deliberately chosen to be
//   insensitive to this bug. It reads the same on broken and fixed RTL, so it
//   isolates the failure: if r7 is wrong while r8 is right, the fault is the
//   extension specifically, and not ori being broken generally, the ALU OR
//   path, or a program that never ran.
//
// INDEPENDENT WITNESS
//   dmem word 0 carries r7 and dmem word 4 carries r8, each stored eight
//   instructions after the value is produced so the read comes cleanly from
//   the register file. Reset leaves word 0 at 0x00000014, so 0x00008000 there
//   proves the store executed and carried the extended value.
//
// CYCLE COUNT
//   19 cycles for the last instruction to retire, zero stalls, zero flushes.
//     15 instructions
//   +  4 cycles of pipeline fill
//   = 19
//   No lw, so the interlock must never fire; no j, so nothing is flushed.
//   Unchanged before and after the fix -- extension is pure combinational
//   width, it costs no cycles either way.
//
// EXPECTED FINAL STATE
//   r7        = 0x00008000     <-- 0xFFFF8000 while ori sign-extends. EVIDENCE.
//   r8        = 0x00000044     positive control, identical either way
//   dmem[0:3] = 0x00008000     <-- 0xFFFF8000 on the broken core
//   dmem[4:7] = 0x00000044
//   stalls    = 0
//
// 0: ori r7, r0, 0x8000     bit 15 SET. Must zero-extend to 0x00008000.
34078000
// 1: nop
00000000
// 2: nop
00000000
// 3: nop
00000000
// 4: ori r8, r0, 0x0044     bit 15 clear: same under either extension
34080044
// 5: nop
00000000
// 6: nop
00000000
// 7: nop
00000000
// 8: sw  r7, 0(r0)          evidence witness into dmem word 0
AC070000
// 9: nop
00000000
// 10: nop
00000000
// 11: nop
00000000
// 12: sw  r8, 4(r0)         control witness into dmem word 4
AC080004
// 13: nop
00000000
// 14: nop
00000000
